    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d136">

                <pb facs="0181" n="97" xml:id="pg97"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72114A/222</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Switzerland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Stovall</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-10-11T19:00:00-04:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 11, 1918, 7 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3106. For Garrett:</p>
                <p>Your unnumbered [<hi rendition="#italic">14</hi>] October 5, 2 p.m. This
                    Government cannot accept the German proposal with regard to the internment or
                    deportation of German civilians in China as stated in your telegram. While this
                    Government does not view with favor the wholesale internment or deportation of
                    Germans residing in China, it desires to remain free to support the same measure
                    of control to be exercised over German civilians in China as the Government of
                    the United States exercises over German civilians in this country.</p>
                <p>Your action in refusing to see Mensing privately is approved.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
